[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m To find the area of triangle \(OAB\) given the vectors \(\overrightarrow{OA} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\overrightarrow{OB} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ -2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}\), we use the cross product method.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m 1. Compute the cross product \(\overrightarrow{OA} \times \overrightarrow{OB}\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m    \overrightarrow{OA} \times \overrightarrow{OB} = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m    \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m    1 & 2 & 3 \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m    -3 & -2 & 1
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m    \end{vmatrix} = \mathbf{i}(2 \cdot 1 - 3 \cdot (-2)) - \mathbf{j}(1 \cdot 1 - 3 \cdot (-3)) + \mathbf{k}(1 \cdot (-2) - 2 \cdot (-3))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m    = \mathbf{i}(2 + 6) - \mathbf{j}(1 + 9) + \mathbf{k}(-2 + 6) = 8\mathbf{i} - 10\mathbf{j} + 4\mathbf{k}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m    So, \(\overrightarrow{OA} \times \overrightarrow{OB} = \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ -10 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1916448)[0m 2. Calculate the magnitude of the cross product:
